  "summary": "Colorful wooden masks used in Paucartambo's annual Virgen del Carmen festival blending indigenous and Catholic elements.",
  "description": "Characterized by exaggerated facial features, vibrant colors, and symbolic designs representing demons, angels, and folk characters, crafted from wood and decorated with paint, hair, and other materials. These masks serve as visual storytelling devices during the festival, preserving syncretic traditions that combine pre-Columbian beliefs with Catholic symbolism.",
